A||N||2||FieroSTETZ||any ideas why i have to add clutch fluid every 2 weeks?||||1||
Z||000000||FieroSTETZ||12-21-2001||10:59 AM||||hi! just wondering, anyone have any idea why my car makes me carry a bottle of dot 3? the clutch pedal goes unresponsive every 2 weeks or so, and i check and see that the resovoir is empty. i was htinking i might have a leak, but cant find any evidence of one.. the clutch master and slave are both new w/ less than 10k||||reg||1
Z||000001||johnt671||12-21-2001||11:20 AM||||From reading other threads on clutches, they say that the master cylinder can leak inside the car and the fluid can be soaked up in the carpet and matting.  Pull the carpet out around the clutch and brake pedals and see if it is wet there.||||reg||1
Z||000002||brharris27370||12-21-2001||04:57 PM||||Mine did that and it was the slave cylinder leaking into the rubber boot.  Buy a GM one, it doesn't cost any more from gmpartsdirect.com than a rebuild does and is a much better unit.  None of my rebuilt ones lasted more than a year and then I learned of <A HREF="http://www.gmpartsdirect.com" TARGET=_blank>www.gmpartsdirect.com</A> ||||reg||1
